    "Reason : 1 - On 07/01/2026 the use of the subdivided house's two self-contained flats on the first floor and one self-contained flat on the second floor was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).  \r\n\r\nThe applicant has submitted insufficient evidence to demonstrate that, on the balance of probabilities, the house's two self-contained flats on the first floor and one self-contained flat on the second floor had been occupied continuously as self-contained dwellings (Class C3) since at least 3 June 2021 (four years prior to the validation date of this Lawful Development Certificate Application) and that continued use to this effect would be lawful.  "
